<p>A federal grand jury in Boston has indicted 10 Indian nationals on one count of conspiracy to commit visa fraud, according to US Justice Department statements cited by the reports. Prosecutors say the case centers on an alleged scheme in which people staged armed robberies at convenience stores, liquor stores, and fast-food restaurants in Massachusetts and elsewhere so clerks could falsely claim to be victims of qualifying crimes when applying for U non-immigrant status, or U visas. All 10 defendants had previously been charged by criminal complaint and released on conditions, while two of them, Rameshbhai Patel and Ronakkumar Patel, were later taken into immigration custody. US authorities said the defendants are subject to deportation after any sentence imposed, and tied the latest indictment to an earlier investigation into alleged organiser Rambhai Patel and alleged getaway driver Balwinder Singh, who were charged in December 2023 and later convicted in May 2025. The case underscores how law enforcement is trying to protect a visa program meant for genuine victims who help investigations.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Dartr6a58nQGEr4xL7kbE9zcuFSvAF2Y9NT9u1fErwfFQ5JBTuJVYKEhSs_LplCXzvsrmcxjciKuinG-TaOeZU0lVfMkFgF0NRHEgFPEWbD7' alt='File photo shows a wooden gavel.— AFP/File' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Stores targeted: Charging documents cited in the reports say the staged robberies hit at least six convenience stores, liquor stores, and fast-food restaurants in Massachusetts and other locations.</li><li>Custody status: Of the 10 defendants, Rameshbhai Patel and Ronakkumar Patel were taken into immigration custody, while the others were previously released on conditions after the criminal complaint.</li><li>Scheme method: The Justice Department said the fake robberies allegedly involved threats with an apparent firearm before cash was taken, allowing clerks to later back up U visa claims as crime victims.</li><li>Program purpose: The U visa is meant for victims of certain crimes who suffered mental or physical abuse and who helped law enforcement investigate or prosecute criminal activity.</li></ul><blockquote>The defendants are subject to deportation upon completion of any sentence imposed. - US Justice Department statement</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Justice Department: Federal prosecutors described the case as a conspiracy to misuse the U visa system through staged robberies, and a grand jury formalized that view in an indictment charging one count of conspiracy to commit visa fraud. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/ten-indian-nationals-indicted-in-us-for-visa-fraud-conspiracy/article70850030.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>US Attorney&#x27;s Office: Officials said all 10 defendants had already faced criminal complaints and had been released on conditions before the indictment, showing that the case has been building over time. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/10-indian-nationals-indicted-in-us-visa-fraud-conspiracy-11341565#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Investigators in earlier case: Authorities linked the new indictments to their earlier investigation of alleged organiser Rambhai Patel and alleged getaway driver Balwinder Singh, signaling that prosecutors view the latest charges as part of a broader organized scheme. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1990558/us-jury-indicts-10-indians-for-visa-fraud-conspiracy-involving-staged-robberies-at-convenience-stores'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1990558/us-jury-indicts-10-indians-for-visa-fraud-conspiracy-involving-staged-robberies-at-convenience-stores'>US jury indicts 10 Indians for visa fraud conspiracy involving staged robberies at convenience stores</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/ten-indian-nationals-indicted-in-us-for-visa-fraud-conspiracy/article70850030.ece'>Ten Indian nationals indicted in U.S. for visa fraud conspiracy</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/10-indian-nationals-indicted-in-us-visa-fraud-conspiracy-11341565#publisher=newsstand'>10 Indian Nationals Indicted In US Visa Fraud Conspiracy</a> - ndtv.com</li></ul>